---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config.mjs';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About The Critical Point — independent financial analysis" lang="en">
  <article class="post">
    <h1 class="post-title">About</h1>
    <div class="post-content">
      <p>This is {SITE.author}'s independent financial analysis. No price predictions — only mechanisms taken apart. The market is a distributed computer run by billions of people, and what I try to do is see what it is computing.</p>
      <p>Topics span equities, currencies, assets, macro, and occasional reflections on order and human nature. Independent, unsponsored, and representing nothing but my own biases. Updated daily; English editions of new articles are published alongside the Chinese originals.</p>
      <h2>How these articles are written</h2>
      <p>Up front: <strong>the articles on this site are generated by AI.</strong> Subject selection, prose, and both language editions come out of an automated pipeline that runs daily. The analytical method and editorial voice it follows are mine — what to write about, what to leave alone, and which frameworks to take a thing apart with — and I set and keep tuning them. I review each piece before it goes out.</p>
      <p>The point of working this way is to publish every day, not to cut corners. But I would rather you not assume every sentence was typed out by hand, so it is stated here.</p>
      <p>On data: the pipeline works to verify market and macro figures against primary sources — official statistical agencies, company filings, exchanges — and drops any number it cannot confirm. Even so, <strong>errors remain possible</strong>. Any figure you intend to act on should be checked against its primary source yourself. If you spot a mistake, <a href="/en/contact">tell me</a> and I will fix it.</p>
      <h2>Content and payment</h2>
      <p>Most articles are free. A few in-depth pieces are <strong>pay-per-article</strong>: the price is shown in USD on the article page, the opening is free to preview, and the full text unlocks instantly after payment. If a free article was valuable to you, you can also <strong>leave a tip</strong> at the end. Payments are processed by Stripe and support major cards.</p>
      <p>For details, see the <a href="/en/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/en/refunds">Refund Policy</a>, or <a href="/en/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
